cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its derived results, please cite it using the
  metadata below, and cite the underlying public datasets separately — their
  version-pinned DOIs are listed in DOWNLOAD_CHECKLIST.md.
title: >-
  sprime-lung-repro: reproducible S' analysis and statistical controls for
  genotype-selective drug vulnerabilities in lung cancer cell lines
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, checksum-guarded reproduction of an S' operational
  drug-response analysis computed from public PRISM (drug response) and DepMap
  (somatic mutation) data for 94 lung cancer cell lines. Builds the S' / pS' /
  delta-pS' metrics per compound-cell-line pair, calls PTEN, CDKN2A, RB1 and
  TP53 genotypes, and runs the statistical controls needed to interpret the
  resulting candidate lists: a label-permutation null, a line-centring
  general-sensitivity control, a per-compound bootstrap confidence-interval
  gate, a literature-blind concordance benchmark, and a DEMETER2 RNAi
  genetic-dependency cross-check. Every input is pinned by figshare version and
  md5; every RNG is seeded; derived tables are written in canonical order so
  runs are reproducible.
type: software
# TODO (maintainer): replace this entity author with named people, adding
# `family-names`, `given-names` and `orcid` for each. Zenodo and the citation
# formats below propagate whatever is recorded here, so a named author list is
# worth adding before minting a release DOI. Kept generic for now to match the
# LICENSE copyright line rather than guess at attribution.
authors:
